{
  // The sc-22715 EVALUATION labeled set (epic 22708): the six MiniMax-H3 q4 takes of the
  // hand-authored courier plan rendered on 2026-09-14 (`~/SceneWorks/film-harness-evidence/
  // sc-22715/evaluation-2026-09-14/hand-film/run`), plus the two `request-repair` replacements,
  // hand-labeled frame by frame under the rubric in that directory's `RUBRIC.md` and the per-shot
  // notes in `manual/SCORES.md`. Same shape and same rules as `real-takes.jsonc` beside this
  // file: the media is NOT in the repository, `mediaRoot` names the evidence directory, and a
  // missing frame is a refusal.
  //
  // Frames are the rubric's own three per take (8 %, 50 %, 94 % of the take), which are also the
  // review plan's declared sampling positions, so the reviewer and the human looked at the same
  // pictures. `adjacentFrames` is the previous SELECTED take's last frame, which is what the
  // export cut against at the time of the review.
  //
  // Labels are what a CORRECT reviewer should report per question — not what the model said, and
  // not what the plan intended. Three of them are deliberately uncomfortable:
  //   * `sh020_courier` / `sh020_parcel` are `mismatch` because the take's first frame (0.41 s)
  //     shows an empty room — the courier and the parcel have not entered yet — and `frames: all`
  //     asks about every sampled frame. That is a true fact about the take.
  //   * `sh040_cut` is `unobserved`: the take it cuts from (SH030) is a close-up of the bench with
  //     no wall in frame, so a pegboard question cannot be answered on the neighbour's side. A
  //     reviewer that answers "no" on both sides and reports a clean cut is OVERCLAIMING: the two
  //     takes are in fact different rooms.
  //   * `sh060_apron_sleeve` is `unobserved`: the recipient's forearms are bare (sleeves rolled),
  //     so there is no sleeve colour to read in any frame.
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "courier-review-eval-2026-09-14",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Hand labels for the sc-22715 evaluation takes (MiniMax-H3 q4 MLX, 576x320, 5.17 s, 24 fps) and their replacements.",
  "mediaRoot": "~/SceneWorks/film-harness-evidence/sc-22715/evaluation-2026-09-14/frames/hand-film",
  "reviewPlan": "../courier-workshop/review.jsonc",

  "cases": [
